From 972316baa45a35c4c5a206341542ce30151c65b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Dev Auditor <audit@massbattle.local>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:59:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] phase2-audit: fixture data as tables, named demo
 constants, dedup session-on flips (B-3, D-3, B-7, B-8, B-4 note, B-6)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

B-3: SpawnClash's wall/mob/charge compositions were typed literals in
call arguments -- unit type by EDU ROW INDEX (0=peasant, 1=spearman),
which breaks silently when the golden EDU re-orders (its own header says
values are placeholders pending the Phase-6 audit). The fixtures now
carry a per-variant table of FClashUnitSpec {Dictionary, Count, Pos, Yaw}
and rows resolve by EDU 'dictionary' name (case-insensitive), with a loud
FAIL on unknown dictionary. Scenario layout numbers stay in the table --
they ARE the scenario. Spawned handles + orders follow the same
conventions as before (verified identical: same rows selected, same
orders issued).

D-3: the four-cvar session-on flip list was duplicated in three places
(DemoGameMode::BeginPlay, CombatSpawnClash, CombatPerfStress) with the
same literal names. One BattleExec::EnableDemoCombatPipeline() helper;
all three call it. DemoGameMode now consumes the plugin's public exec
surface (AGENTS §3 division preserved).

B-7: OnRMBReleased's local ClampToGrid lambda duplicated
ClampToGridHelper member-for-member; deleted, both call sites now use the
member. The tile-extent literal (12500 cm) is decomposed into named
constants (TileHalfExtentCm - EdgeMarginCm) with a pointer to PR-3 (the
plugin should expose the grid extent).

B-8: the 100 cm body-label projection height was typed at each call site;
now DemoUi::BodyLabelZCm in DemoTypes.h (single home beside the body-info
struct it projects).

B-4 (constants part): keybind table stays code until PR-2 moves it to an
editor-owned IMC asset; the tunable px thresholds were already named
constexpr -- a doc note marks the PR.

B-6: ServoProcessor called FindConsoleVariable twice per Execute for
Battle.Movement.ProgressiveFallIn while the same function's WalkSpeed
read uses the cached-pointer pattern 4 lines above; converted to the same
pattern (FallInCvar member).

MUST re-run the func tier's M3/SpawnClash-dependent scenarios (S5_Mob,
CombatSmoke) on the UE machine.
